comments.body:
@kahyunnam Thank you for the detailed review and the SM100 measurements — especially for catching the dropped parameter validation and the stale CPU oracle.

Addressed in dcc6d4c8b:

- passed `indices` through the compact top-p sampler, preserving the original `top_p` length validation and avoiding compact-row expansion;
- added the ≥65536-vocab indexed fast-path regression covering boundary ties, duplicate indices, tensor `top_k`/`top_p`, int64 output, and fixed-seed equality with the expanded non-indexed call;
- updated both `top_k_max` docstrings and the stale test comment;
- updated the chain CPU oracle and middle-rejection expectation, and added an α=0.5 GPU regression that checks the accepted and emitted counters match;
- updated the PR description with the fixed-seed compatibility note, the lower cross-version `output_accepted_token_num` note, and the SM100 performance context (including that it was not measured on B200).

The focused new/updated cases pass (8 tests), the affected existing fast-path/chain cases pass (18 tests), and pre-commit passes on all changed files. Thanks again!
